# Working with AI

#### You just engaged with an AI chatbot to help optimize a computer system, exploring different actions to improve performance. 
#### This activity demonstrated how AI can be a valuable tool for analyzing problems, brainstorming solutions, and considering different optimization strategies.



<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; width: 90%; margin: 20px auto;">
<p style = "font-size:14pt;"><strong>Key Takeaways:</strong></p>
  <ul style = "font-size:14pt;">
    <li><b>A Great Tool for Problem-Solving</b> – AI can provide helpful suggestions, generate ideas, and offer alternative solutions that you may not have considered.</li><br>
    <li><b>Not Always Perfect</b> – AI responses are based on patterns and data, but they aren’t always accurate or the best fit for a situation. It’s important to evaluate responses critically and use your own judgment.</li><br>
    <li><b>Works Best with Clear Prompts</b> – The way you ask questions affects the quality of the response. Being specific and refining your prompts can lead to better, more relevant answers.</li><br>
    <li><b>Encourages Inquiry-Based Thinking</b> – Instead of simply giving answers, AI can help guide exploration, prompting deeper analysis and discussion.</li><br>
    <li><b>Requires Responsible Use</b> – When using AI tools with students, it’s important to establish guidelines around ethical use, data privacy, and responsible interactions.</li>
</ul>
</div>

#### As we move into reflection, think about how AI supported your learning and how you might use it effectively in your teaching practice.
